A standard Jenkinsfile contains these core sections: 
[1] (https://www.jenkins.io/doc/book/pipeline/jenkinsfile/)
pipeline: The outer block enclosing all pipeline definition code.
agent: Defines where the pipeline or stage will run (e.g., any available machine).
stages: A container sequence for one or more stage blocks.
stage: A distinct phase like Build, Test, or Deploy.
steps: The actual tasks executed inside a stage
